    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    ops = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(next(it))\n        C = int(next(it))\n        verts = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(K)]\n        ops.append((C, verts))\n    \n    # Process operations in increasing order of edge weight\n    ops.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    size = [1] * (N + 1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx = find(x)\n        ry = find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if size[rx] < size[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        size[rx] += size[ry]\n        return True\n    \n    total_cost = 0\n    for C, verts in ops:\n        # Gather unique representatives of the vertices in this clique\n        leaders = set()\n        for v in verts:\n            leaders.add(find(v))\n        if len(leaders) > 1:\n            # Connecting c components requires c-1 edges of weight C\n            total_cost += C * (len(leaders) - 1)\n            it_l = iter(leaders)\n            first = next(it_l)\n            for other in it_l:\n                union(first, other)\n    \n    # Check if the whole graph is connected\n    if size[find(1)] == N:\n        print(total_cost)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n```",
