      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth for deep DSU structures if necessary\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10**6)\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once for efficiency\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(input_data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    \n    # We use Kruskal's algorithm. \n    # Each operation i defines a clique with weight C_i.\n    # To form a MST, we only need to connect vertices within each set S_i\n    # using (K_i - 1) edges of weight C_i.\n    # We sort the operations by weight C_i.\n    \n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(next(it))\n        C = int(next(it))\n        S = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(K)]\n        edges.append((C, S))\n        \n    # Sort operations by weight\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    # DSU (Disjoint Set Union) to track connected components\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i:\n            return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n\n    def union(i, j):\n        root_i = find(i)\n        root_j = find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j:\n            parent[root_i] = root_j\n            return True\n        return False\n\n    total_weight = 0\n    num_edges_added = 0\n    \n    for cost, nodes in edges:\n        # For each set, we try to connect consecutive nodes.\n        # However, connecting every node to the next in the set takes O(K_i).\n        # To optimize, we only need to connect nodes that aren't already in the same component.\n        # Specifically, we can connect nodes[0] to nodes[1], nodes[1] to nodes[2]...\n        # but if nodes[j] and nodes[j+1] are already connected via a cheaper path, \n        # we don't add the edge.\n        \n        # Standard Kruskal logic: \n        # For a set of vertices with cost C, we can potentially add (K-1) edges.\n        # We iterate through the set and union nodes.\n        first_node = nodes[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(nodes)):\n            current_node = nodes[i]\n            # While the nodes are not in the same component, union them.\n            # Note: We must check all pairs (nodes[i], nodes[i+1]) because \n            # intermediate nodes might have been connected by cheaper edges already.\n            if union(first_node, current_node):\n                total_weight += cost\n                num_edges_added += 1\n            else:\n                # If nodes[0] and nodes[i] are already connected, they might be connected\n                # to nodes[i+1] later. We keep nodes[i] as a potential bridge.\n                # Actually, simply attempting to union nodes[i] with nodes[0] is sufficient.\n                pass\n                \n    # Check if the graph is connected (MST must have N-1 edges)\n    if num_edges_added == N - 1:\n        print(total_weight)\n    else:\n        print(\"-1\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
