    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Use fast I/O\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    t = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        a = list(map(int, input_data[idx : idx + n]))\n        idx += n\n        \n        # Precompute prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries\n        prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n        for i in range(n):\n            prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + a[i]\n            \n        max_diff = 0\n        \n        # Iterate through all possible divisors k of n\n        # k represents the number of boxes per truck\n        for k in range(1, n // 2 + 1):\n            if n % k == 0:\n                min_weight = -1\n                max_weight = -1\n                \n                # Check each truck's total weight for the current k\n                for i in range(0, n, k):\n                    # Sum of boxes from index i to i+k-1\n                    current_weight = prefix_sum[i + k] - prefix_sum[i]\n                    \n                    if min_weight == -1 or current_weight < min_weight:\n                        min_weight = current_weight\n                    if max_weight == -1 or current_weight > max_weight:\n                        max_weight = current_weight\n                \n                diff = max_weight - min_weight\n                if diff > max_diff:\n                    max_diff = diff\n        \n        # Edge case: If n=1, or only one truck possible (k=n), max_diff is 0.\n        # The loop above handles all k up to n/2.\n        # For k=n, max_weight - min_weight is always 0.\n        \n        results.append(str(max_diff))\n    \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
