    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The term \"roundabout production\" (or *Produktionsumweg*) was popularized by the Austrian economist Eugen von Böhm-Bawerk to describe the process where resources are first used to create capital goods (like tools or machinery), which are then used to produce final consumer goods more efficiently. This method is more time-consuming than direct production but results in a higher overall output of goods. Therefore, it specifically refers to the indirect path of production involving capital accumulation.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
