    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The balanced budget multiplier measures the net change in equilibrium GDP resulting from an increase in government spending that is exactly offset by an equal increase in taxes. Because the marginal propensity to consume (MPC) applies to only the portion of income that is not taxed away, the positive spending multiplier and the negative tax multiplier sum to exactly 1. All other multipliers listed (spending, investment, money, etc.) equal \\(1/(1-\\text{MPC})\\) or an analogous expression strictly greater than 1, while the elasticity of the vertical long-run aggregate supply curve equals zero.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "provider": "nadir",
      "token_usage": {}
