      "generated_answer": "To determine Miss Lane's **Gross Income** and **Adjusted Gross Income (AGI)**, we use the relationship between these tax components. Taxable Income is calculated as:\n\n$$\n\\text{Taxable Income} = \\text{AGI} - \\text{Exemptions} - \\text{Itemized Deductions (Non-business Expenses)}\n$$\n\nGiven:\n- Taxable Income = \\$15,000\n- Exemptions = \\$1,500\n- Non-business Expenses = \\$3,000\n- Business Expenses = \\$6,000 (deducted from Gross Income to compute AGI)\n\nFirst, solve for **AGI**:\n$$\n15,000 = \\text{AGI} - 1,500 - 3,000 \\implies \\text{AGI} = 15,000 + 4,500 = 19,500\n$$\n\nNext, compute **Gross Income**:\n$$\n\\text{AGI} = \\text{Gross Income} - \\text{Business Expenses} \\implies 19,500 = \\text{Gross Income} - 6,000 \\implies \\text{Gross Income} = 25,500\n$$\n\nThe correct answer is **Option A**.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{A}\n$$",
