    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10237",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Design a square key for a 3 in. diameter shaft to withstand a torque of 30,000 lbs.-in. The design stresses in shear and bearing can be safely taken as 11,000 psi and 22,000 psi, respectively.\n\nOptions: \nA. thickness = 1/2 in., width = 1/2 in., length = 3 in.\nB. thickness = 3/4 in., width = 3/4 in., length = 2.5 in.\nC. thickness = 1 in., width = 1 in., length = 2 in.\nD. thickness = 1/2 in., width = 3/4 in., length = 2.5 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To design the key, we check both shear and bearing stresses. Shear stress: τ = T / (r · A_s), where A_s = L · t (t = thickness), r = d/2 = 1.5 in. Bearing stress: σ_b = T / (r · A_b), where A_b = L · (w/2) (w = width), assuming contact on one flank.\n\nFor option D (t = 0.5 in, w = 0.75 in, L = 2.5 in):  \nτ = 30,000 / (1.5 × 2.5 × 0.5) = 16,000 psi > 11,000 psi → **fails shear**, so not D.  \nOption A (t = w = 0.5 in, L = 3 in): τ = 30,000 / (1.5 × 3 × 0.5) = 13,333 psi > 11,000 psi → fails shear.  \nOption B (t = w = 0.75 in, L = 2.5 in): τ = 30,000 / (1.5 × 2.5 × 0.75) = 10,667 psi ≤ 11,000 psi (OK); bearing: σ_b = 30,000 / (1.5 × 2.5 × 0.375) = 21,333 psi ≤ 22,000 psi (OK).  \nOption C (t = w = 1 in, L = 2 in): τ = 30,000 / (1.5 × 2 × 1) = 10,000 psi (OK), bearing = 30,000 / (1.5 × 2 × 0.5) = 20,000 psi (OK), but B is smaller and still safe.\n\nSince both B and C are safe, but B uses less material and meets both criteria, **B is the most appropriate design**.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
