      "generated_answer": "To find the correct key dimensions, we use the formulas for shear stress ($\\tau = \\frac{2T}{dWL}$) and bearing stress ($\\sigma_b = \\frac{4T}{dHL}$). For a 3-inch shaft, the standard square key size is $W = H = 3/4$ inch. Plugging these values into the shear formula: $11,000 = \\frac{2(30,000)}{(3)(0.75)L}$, we solve for $L \\approx 2.42$ inches, which aligns with the standard length of 2.5 inches.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
