    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the number of bits required to represent 110 different codewords in a binary system, we calculate the minimum number $ n $ such that $ 2^n \\geq 110 $. This gives $ n = 7 $, since $ 2^6 = 64 < 110 $ and $ 2^7 = 128 \\geq 110 $.\n\nNow, to evaluate the **efficiency** of the binary system compared to a decimal system, we consider the concept of **information entropy**. The minimal number of bits required to represent 110 codewords is $ \\log_2(110) \\approx 6.78 $ bits. Since the system uses 7 bits, the **efficiency** can be defined as the ratio of the minimal bits required to the actual bits used:\n\n$$\n\\text{Efficiency} = \\frac{\\log_2(110)}{7} \\times 100 \\approx \\frac{6.78}{7} \\times 100 \\approx 97\\%\n$$\n\nThis means that the binary system is approximately 97% efficient in terms of how much of the bit space is used to represent the 110 codewords.\n\n---\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{H}\n$$",
