    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Fouriertransformmethods to find the time-domain responseof a network having a system function [(j2\\omega) / (1 + 2j\\omega)], ifthe input is V(t) =cost (For asinusodialinputcost, the Fourier transform is \\pi[\\delta (\\omega + 1) + \\delta (\\omega - 1)] ).\n\nOptions: \nA. (4/5)cost - (2/5) sin t\nB. (3/4)cost - (1/4)sint\nC. (2/5)cost + (4/5) sin t\nD. cost + sint\nE. (3/5)cost + (1/5)sint\nF. (4/5)cost + (2/5) sin t\nG. (1/5)cost - (3/5)sint\nH. (1/2)cost + (1/2)sint\nI. (1/3)cost - (2/3)sint\nJ. (2/5)cost - (4/5) sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the time-domain response of the system with transfer function $ H(j\\omega) = \\frac{j2\\omega}{1 + 2j\\omega} $ to the input $ V(t) = \\cos t $, we use the Fourier transform method.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Input in Frequency Domain\nThe Fourier transform of $ \\cos t $ is:\n$$\n\\mathcal{F}\\{\\cos t\\} = \\pi[\\delta(\\omega + 1) + \\delta(\\omega - 1)]\n$$\nThis represents two impulses at $ \\omega = \\pm 1 $, each scaled by $ \\pi $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Multiply by Frequency Response\nThe output in the frequency domain is:\n$$\nY(j\\omega) = H(j\\omega) \\cdot \\pi[\\delta(\\omega + 1) + \\delta(\\omega - 1)]\n$$\nSo the output becomes:\n$$\nY(j\\omega) = \\pi[H(j1)\\delta(\\omega - 1) + H(-j1)\\delta(\\omega + 1)]\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Evaluate $ H(j\\omega) $ at $ \\omega = \\pm 1 $\n$$\nH(j1) = \\frac{j2}{1 + j2} = \\frac{4 + j2}{5}, \\quad H(-j1) = \\frac{-j2}{1 - j2} = \\frac{4 - j2}{5}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Inverse Fourier Transform\nThe inverse Fourier transform of the output is:\n$$\ny(t) = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ \\frac{4 - j2}{5} e^{-jt} + \\frac{4 + j2}{5} e^{jt} \\right]\n$$\n\nExpanding this:\n$$\ny(t) = \\frac{1}{10} \\left[ (4 - j2)e^{-jt} + (4 + j2)e^{jt} \\right]\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula:\n$$\ne^{jt} + e^{-jt} = 2\\cos t, \\quad e^{jt} - e^{-jt} = 2j\\sin t\n$$\n\nSimplifying:\n$$\ny(t) = \\frac{1}{10} \\left[ 8\\cos t - 4\\sin t \\right] = \\frac{4}{5}\\cos t - \\frac{2}{5}\\sin t\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{A}\n$$",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
