    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For similarity, the model and prototype must match the Froude number (since gravity is the dominant force, and viscous effects are negligible for open-channel flow over a sluice gate). With scale ratio $ L_r = 1/20 $, the Froude number similarity gives $ V_r = \\sqrt{L_r} = 1/\\sqrt{20} $, and discharge scales as $ Q_r = A_r V_r = L_r^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{L_r} = L_r^{5/2} = (1/20)^{5/2} $. Thus, $ Q_p = Q_m / L_r^{5/2} = 0.5 \\times 20^{5/2} = 0.5 \\times (20^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{20}) = 0.5 \\times 400 \\times 4.472 \\approx 894.4~\\text{m}^3/\\text{s} $. The head in the model is $ h_m = h_p / 20 = 1~\\text{m} $, but the question only asks for prototype discharge.\n\n$\\boxed{E}$",
