ld\nH. Enforcing strict rationing of food supplies\nI. Instituting a new Republican Calendar\nJ. The conscription of huge armies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The policy of de-Christianization alienated large segments of the population, particularly peasants and Catholics, fueling major internal revolts like the Vendée uprising that diverted troops and resources from fighting external invaders. Other policies, such as mass conscription, merit-based promotions, economic controls, and the Terror, directly strengthened military mobilization and internal security against foreign coalitions. The Republican Calendar and slavery abolition had minimal or tangential effects on European defense, but de-Christianization was actively harmful.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
