ld\nH. Enforcing strict rationing of food supplies\nI. Instituting a new Republican Calendar\nJ. The conscription of huge armies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the change **least beneficial to the defense of France** during the radical phase (1793–1794), when Robespierre led the Committee of Public Safety. While many listed policies (e.g., conscription, price controls to maintain domestic stability, merit-based promotion to enhance military effectiveness, rationing to support the army) directly supported war efforts or internal security, **instituting a new Republican Calendar** (I) was largely symbolic and had no practical impact on defense capabilities—it did not improve military organization, morale, logistics, or recruitment. Its primary purpose was ideological and cultural, not strategic.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
