ld\nH. Enforcing strict rationing of food supplies\nI. Instituting a new Republican Calendar\nJ. The conscription of huge armies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nDuring the radical phase of the French Revolution, Robespierre's policy of **de-Christianization** was least beneficial to the defense of France because it alienated the deeply religious rural population and created internal divisions that fueled counter-revolutionary movements like the War in the Vendée. In contrast, measures like the *levée en masse* (conscription) and price controls were directly aimed at strengthening the military and ensuring social stability during wartime. While other options like the Reign of Terror were controversial, de-Christianization specifically undermined national unity without providing a strategic military advantage.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
