    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Sugar Act of 1764 aimed to raise revenue through duties on colonial trade while also regulating and protecting British commerce, reflecting mercantilist principles. Among the options, protective tariffs established during the Industrial Revolution served a similar dual purpose of generating government revenue and shielding domestic industries through trade regulations. Therefore, the goals presented in the excerpt align most closely with protective tariffs.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
