ter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**.\n\nIn both 1952 (during the Korean War) and 1968 (during the Vietnam War), the American electorate felt exhausted by foreign conflicts and domestic social upheaval, leading to a desire for stability. This sentiment benefited Republican candidates Dwight D. Eisenhower and Richard Nixon, who both campaigned on restoring order and \"peace with honor.\" Consequently, the public shifted toward more conservative leadership to escape the perceived chaos associated with the incumbent Democratic administrations.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
