n Africans utilized trading contacts with Europeans to spread their cultural influence throughout Europe.\nJ. Sub-Saharan Africans engaged in trade with Europeans to acquire new agricultural techniques.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nThe quote from Rodney highlights European exploitation through trade, but for Sub-Saharan Africans in 1450-1750 C.E., European contacts were most important for acquiring firearms in the Atlantic slave trade, enabling states like Asante and Dahomey to consolidate power via the gun-slave cycle. Option E overstates immediate industrial collapse, which occurred later. Other options misrepresent trade dynamics, such as sole reliance on Europeans or primary focus on education/foodstuffs.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
