      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}.\n\nThe conflict primarily stemmed from the Safavid Empire’s promotion and adherence to Twelver Shi'ism, which the Sunni Ottoman (and to a lesser extent, the Mughal) rulers viewed as a heretical \"evil innovation.\" The provided text highlights this religious antagonism by citing the need to \"exterminate\" those who introduce such innovations, referring directly to the sectarian divide.",
