      "generated_answer": "The passage emphasizes the socialist transformation of agriculture through collectivization to prevent rural class polarization and consolidate the worker-peasant alliance. Mao's advocacy for eliminating individual and rich-peasant economies aligns with the Soviet model of forced collectivization under Stalin, which sought to eradicate class distinctions and establish state-controlled agricultural production. While other socialist ideologies (e.g., B, C) emphasize democratic or gradual reforms, Mao's approach directly mirrors Stalin’s authoritarian communist policies. \n\n\\boxed{A}",
