    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. Reconstruction**.\n\nThe desegregation of schools was a response to the unfulfilled promises of the Reconstruction era, specifically the 14th Amendment's guarantee of \"equal protection of the laws\" which was undermined by the \"separate but equal\" doctrine of *Plessy v. Ferguson*. While the Civil War ended slavery, the subsequent era failed to secure the civil and social equality promised to African Americans, leading to the legal challenges of the 1950s.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
