    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed the failure to uphold the equal protection promised by the Fourteenth Amendment, which was central to the Reconstruction era (1865–1877). Despite constitutional amendments during Reconstruction, systemic segregation and disenfranchisement persisted, leading to the 1954 ruling. The unfulfilled promises of Reconstruction directly contextualize the need for desegregation. \n\n\\boxed{D}",
