      "generated_answer": "The law was a Pennsylvania \"personal liberty law\" meant to criminalize the kidnapping of free Black people, and it directly conflicted with the federal Fugitive Slave Act of 1793. This created a legal and political struggle over whether state laws could override federal slave-catching requirements, a conflict that eventually reached the Supreme Court in Prigg v. Pennsylvania (1842).\n\n\\boxed{E}",
