    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The law criminalizes the removal or seduction of Black people (referred to as \"negro or mulatto\") from Pennsylvania with intent to enslave them, indicating it was designed to protect Black residents from being kidnapped and sold into slavery—even though Pennsylvania had abolished slavery by 1780. This reflects the tension between Northern states like Pennsylvania, which had moved toward abolition (however limited or gradual), and Southern states where slavery remained legal and economically entrenched, especially regarding the enforcement of fugitive slave laws and protection of enslaved people across state lines. Although the law appears abolitionist on its face, it was also a response to Southern demands for compliance with federal fugitive slave laws and反映出 broader national conflict over slavery’s expansion and enforcement.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
