      "generated_answer": "The Pennsylvania law of 1826 criminalized efforts to kidnap or transport Black individuals out of the state for enslavement elsewhere. This reflects the broader national tension between Northern states, which increasingly opposed slavery and sought to protect free Black populations, and Southern states, which relied on slavery and often pressured Northern states to comply with pro-slavery practices. The law specifically targeted actions that facilitated the Southern slave system, highlighting the sectional divide. \n\n\\boxed{G}",
