    "global index": "MathQA_1215",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if two dice are thrown together , the probability of getting a doublet on the dice is\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 1 / 5\nC. 1 / 4\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 1 / 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When two dice are thrown, there are $6 \\times 6 = 36$ equally likely outcomes. A doublet means both dice show the same number: (1,1), (2,2), ..., (6,6), which gives 6 favorable outcomes. Thus, the probability is $ \\frac{6}{36} = \\frac{1}{6} $.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
