      "generated_answer": "Let the wire of length $L = 12$ be cut at a point $x$ (where $0 < x < 12$), creating two pieces of lengths $x$ and $12-x$. The longer piece, $L_{max} = \\max(x, 12-x)$, forms the perimeter of a square with side $s = \\frac{L_{max}}{4}$, so its area is $A = (\\frac{L_{max}}{4})^2$. We require $A > 4$, which means $\\frac{L_{max}}{4} > 2$, or $L_{max} > 8$. Since $L_{max}$ is the longer piece, this occurs if $x > 8$ or $12-x > 8$ (which means $x < 4$); the total length of these favorable intervals is $(12-8) + (4-0) = 8$, and the total length of the wire is 12, so the probability is $8/12 = 2/3$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
