    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability that Simone loses no more than 1/3 of her original investment, we first determine the total investment, which is $3k$. Losing no more than 1/3 means her loss must be $\\le k$; since each investment is worth $k$, this occurs if 0 or 1 investment becomes worthless.\n\nUsing the binomial probability formula $P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$ with $n=3$ and $p=0.2$:\n- $P(0 \\text{ losses}) = (0.8)^3 = 0.512$\n- $P(1 \\text{ loss}) = 3 \\times (0.2)^1 \\times (0.8)^2 = 3 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.64 = 0.384$\nTotal probability = $0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896$, which is approximately 90%.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
