    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Square root of pq/n indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Standard error of mean\nB. Standard error of difference of means\nC. Standard error of proportions\nD. Standard error of difference in proportions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The standard error of a sample proportion \\(p\\) (where \\(q = 1-p\\)) is given by the formula \\(\\sqrt{pq/n}\\). This follows directly from the binomial variance formula \\(\\text{Var}(X) = npq\\), after dividing by \\(n^2\\) and taking the square root. The other listed quantities have different expressions (e.g., SE of a difference of proportions includes two such terms under a single radical).\n\nThus the indicated quantity matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
