    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the whole-tone scale is incorrect?\n\nOptions: \nA. The interval between adjacent notes in the whole-tone scale is a major second\nB. Debussy's piano prelude 'Voiles' made extensive use of the whole-tone scale\nC. If a whole-tone scale has a B flat, it must also contain an E\nD. Within an octave range, the whole-tone scale contains intervals of major second, major third, augmented fourth, major sixth, and major seventh\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
