      "generated_answer": "The provided context directly addresses this question in its description of Part 3 (\"The Western War\"). There, Wells explicitly states that new technologies have transformed warfare, rendering formations and cavalry obsolete while making artillery \"the most essential instrument of the war.\"\n\nThis is presented as a key observation from his visit to the Western Front, in contrast to outdated military thinking.\n\n\\boxed{artillery}",
