      "generated_answer": "According to H. G. Wells in *War and the Future*, written in September 1916, **artillery is now the most essential instrument of the war**. He emphasizes that new technologies have transformed warfare, rendering traditional tactics like disciplined formations and cavalry obsolete. While he notes the emerging importance of tanks and aerial dominance, he specifically identifies artillery as paramount in the contemporary (1916) conduct of war.  \n\n\\boxed{artillery}",
