    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The context directly identifies Fanshawe as the character who “lags behind the search because of his weak constitution and his slow horse.” This is contrasted with Walcott (the skilled rider enlisted by Melmoth) and is consistent with Fanshawe’s earlier description as a reclusive, physically frail intellectual. No other character is linked to these traits.\n\n\\boxed{Fanshawe}",
