    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Holmes refuses Watson’s examination to prevent Watson from discovering that his illness is a feigned ruse. His starvation and claims of infectiousness were deliberate deceptions to maintain secrecy and lull Watson into believing he was truly dying. Allowing Watson to examine him would have exposed the absence of real symptoms and ruined Holmes’s plan to trap Culverton Smith.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{To prevent Watson from discovering that his illness is a ruse and exposing the trap he is setting for Culverton Smith.}}",
