    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Holmes refused to let Watson examine him because he was not actually sick and needed to maintain the ruse of being near death. He feared that Watson, being a medical doctor, would immediately discover that his symptoms were feigned and that he was merely starving himself. By claiming the disease was highly infectious, Holmes ensured Watson would keep his distance and remain a believable witness to the upcoming confession.\n\n\\boxed{Holmes feigned the illness to trick Culverton Smith into a confession and knew that Watson, a doctor, would immediately discover the ruse if allowed to examine him.}",
