    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The provided context contains the opening of Poe's \"The Cask of Amontillado,\" which concludes (outside the excerpt) with the narrator's Latin phrase \"In pace requiescat!\" after entombing Fortunato. This is a slight inversion of the standard liturgical phrase \"requiescat in pace,\" a prayerful wish that the deceased find eternal rest. It is the source of the common English abbreviation \"RIP.\"\n\n\\boxed{May he rest in peace (Lat.)}",
