      "generated_answer": "\"In pace requiescat\" is a Latin phrase meaning \"May he rest in peace.\"  \nIt is commonly used as a benediction for the deceased, especially on tombstones or in funeral contexts.  \nIn *The Cask of Amontillado*, it appears at the story’s end, irony-laden, as Montresor finishes recounting his murder of Fortunato.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{May he rest in peace}}",
