      "generated_answer": "Based on the context provided, Benedict Arnold's death at the Battle of Quebec led to the British victory of General Burgoyne over Horatio Gates at the Battles of Saratoga. This resulted in the failure of both the American and French Revolutions, meaning the Napoleonic Wars never occurred. Consequently, the United States remained British colonies, and figures like Napoleon and Wellington never rose to their historical positions of supreme power.\n\n\\boxed{His death led to a British victory at Saratoga, causing the American and French Revolutions to fail and preventing the Napoleonic Wars. Consequently, the United States remained a British colony, and historical figures like Napoleon and Arthur Wellesley never attained their famous titles or ranks.}",
