    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An injunctive message can block a negative outcome of this process through the \"boomerang effect.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The described dynamic is a core prediction of the focus theory of normative conduct. When a purely descriptive norm is conveyed (e.g., “most residents use X kWh”), individuals already below the norm often increase their consumption—the classic boomerang effect. Pairing the descriptive information with an injunctive cue (approval or disapproval) eliminates that unintended upward shift, thereby protecting the desired behavior.\n\nThus the process whose negative side-effect is neutralized is social-norms marketing (or descriptive-norm messaging).\n\n\\boxed{social norms mktg (descr. norms)\n}",
      "success": true,
      "provider": "nadir",
      "token_usage": {}
    },
